    "title": "Moore's Season High Lifts UM to Road Win Over CBU - NewsBreak",
    "text": "6 days ago MEMPHIS, Tenn. – Montevallo men's basketball improves to a 4-1 start in Gulf South Conference action after a 75-54 win over Christian Brothers on the road. After the first bucket of the game, Montevallo held CBU scoreless for the first eight minutes of the game to take an early 11-3 lead at the 12:03 mark with seven early points from Brandon Fussell. At the 8:20 mark of the first half, Derek Moore began what would be 10-straight points for Montevallo with a 3-for-3 mark from the field to give Montevallo a 30-15 lead with four minutes before the break. Reese Gurner scored the final four points of the half for the Falcons and stretched the lead to 36-18 heading into the locker room. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
